@DRIFTLESS

vor 17 Stunden

Lots of people still dismiss AI as ''just a language model.'' I've been building, testing and cursing with it since November 2022, and I keep having to update what I think is possible. Faster every time.



One developer is building open alternatives to seven Adobe apps, Photoshop and Premiere included, with Claude. Early versions, sure, but that's ONE person. AI is helping reverse-engineer games like Halo and GTA Vice City so they run in a browser tab. Anthropic shared a case where Claude worked on a software project on its own for over 18 hours. Meanwhile most people are still discovering it can write an email.



The next generation is already knocking the door down while we haven't even caught up with what the current models can do.



I think we mostly underestimate what exponential means. Get 1 euro today, 2 tomorrow, then 4, 8, 16. Day 10: 512. Day 20: half a million. Day 30: 536 million. Day 31: over a BILLION. More in one day than all 30 days before it combined. Nothing changed in the deal, the math just kept going while you were still processing the half million.



AI doesn't follow a neat calendar like that, but my gut says we're somewhere halfway through the month. Now imagine this ever smarter AI doing more and more of the work on the next AI. That's what's so insane about this moment: we already can't keep up, and the wildest part hasn't even started.



We might be building something that outgrows us intellectually. But hey, yesterday it still made a reasoning error.





